DISTRICT POPULATION ANALYSIS AND THEMATIC MAPPING PROJECT
Group 17
1. Project Description
This project demonstrates how Python programming and Geographic Information Systems (GIS) can be used to analyse and visualize district population data in Uganda.
The system uses population statistics and geographical boundary data to generate a thematic map, a population comparison chart and statistical summaries.
2. Project Objectives
Load district population data from a CSV file.
Load geographical boundaries from a GeoJSON file.
Match population data with geographical boundaries.
Calculate population statistics.
Generate an automatic thematic map.
Produce a population comparison chart and PDF report.
3. Technologies Used
Python
PyCharm
GeoPandas
Pandas
Matplotlib
GIS and GeoJSON data
4. Study Districts
The project analyses five districts:
Wakiso
Kampala
Mukono
Jinja
Masaka
